WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.695 --> 00:00:16.736
went straight to Mount Potalaka.

2
00:00:19.178 --> 00:00:21.781
The bodhisattva Guanyin was in her garden.

3
00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:25.844
"Hello, Wukong.

4
00:00:26.524 --> 00:00:27.805
How is the journey going?"

5
00:00:29.687 --> 00:00:30.648
threw up his hands.

6
00:00:31.008 --> 00:00:32.549
"The Tang Monk is crazy!"

7
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.531
"Why?" asked the bodhisattva.

8
00:00:36.631 --> 00:00:39.313
"He told me to leave," said the monkey.

9
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:42.675
"He was mad because I was going to hurt some robbers."

10
00:00:44.536 --> 00:00:47.297
frowned. "It's wrong to hurt people, Wukong.

11
00:00:47.658 --> 00:00:48.338
You know that."

12
00:00:50.059 --> 00:00:52.961
"I hurt demons all the time," said Wukong.

13
00:00:52.981 --> 00:00:56.583
"That's different," said Guanyin.

14
00:00:56.603 --> 00:01:01.149
"Demons are evil, and you're doing a good thing when you get rid of them.

15
00:01:02.349 --> 00:01:04.450
But you must not hurt people."

16
00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:09.411
The monkey sat down and put his head in his hands.

17
00:01:10.931 --> 00:01:13.012
Bodhisattva, you're right."

18
00:01:13.252 --> 00:01:14.512
He started to cry.

19
00:01:14.572 --> 00:01:16.873
"This is terrible.

20
00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:20.734
Now I'll never reach the Western Paradise with the Tang Monk.

21
00:01:21.854 --> 00:01:23.875
I wanted to earn forgiveness."

22
00:01:23.895 --> 00:01:28.460
"Don't cry, Wukong," said Guanyin.

23
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.842
"You will still help the Tang Monk reach the Western Paradise.

24
00:01:33.003 --> 00:01:34.303
will need your help soon.

25
00:01:35.284 --> 00:01:38.046
In the meantime you may stay here with me."

26
00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:45.750
dropped the bags.

27
00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:50.052
"Let's rest here," he said.

28
00:01:50.072 --> 00:01:51.913
"I'm starving."

29
00:01:53.194 --> 00:01:56.276
The Tang Monk climbed down from his horse and stretched.

30
00:01:59.296 --> 00:02:03.077
The horse drank from a stream while Bajie looked in a bag.

31
00:02:03.097 --> 00:02:05.858
"We're out of rice," said the pig.

32
00:02:05.878 --> 00:02:10.099
"We'll have to beg for food somewhere," said Wujing.

33
00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:11.599
He looked at the monk.

34
00:02:11.619 --> 00:02:15.360
"Master, you wait here while Bajie and I find a village."

35
00:02:17.121 --> 00:02:19.161
The monk's two companions flew off.

36
00:02:21.522 --> 00:02:25.283
The monk sat down in the grass next to the road and closed his eyes.

37
00:02:26.703 --> 00:02:28.984
He had nearly dozed off when he heard a voice.

38
00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:35.584
"Master!" It was Wukong.

39
00:02:36.946 --> 00:02:38.807
Tang Monk glared at the monkey.

40
00:02:38.827 --> 00:02:41.389
"Why are you here, Wukong?"

41
00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.811
The monkey fell to his knees.

42
00:02:43.831 --> 00:02:47.534
"I'm begging you—please let me join you again."

43
00:02:47.554 --> 00:02:50.236
"No," said the monk.

44
00:02:50.256 --> 00:02:52.378
"You're evil, Wukong.

45
00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:54.840
You can't go to the Western Paradise with me.

46
00:02:55.781 --> 00:02:58.543
Now leave before I recite the Tight Headband spell!"

47
00:03:00.536 --> 00:03:01.637
monkey was furious.

48
00:03:03.898 --> 00:03:06.379
He pulled out his iron bar, which quickly grew.

49
00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:10.581
Before the monk could recite the spell, Wukong struck.

50
00:03:13.742 --> 00:03:14.783
He knocked out the monk.

51
00:03:15.803 --> 00:03:18.784
Quickly, the monkey grabbed the bags and then vanished.

52
00:03:20.645 --> 00:03:22.666
Wujing and Bajie soon returned.

53
00:03:23.707 --> 00:03:26.668
They found the Tang Monk sitting by the road, rubbing his head.

54
00:03:29.052 --> 00:03:30.733
"Master!" cried Wujing.

55
00:03:30.753 --> 00:03:31.754
"What happened?"

56
00:03:31.774 --> 00:03:33.935
"Where are the bags?"

57
00:03:34.295 --> 00:03:36.016
asked Bajie, looking around.

58
00:03:36.036 --> 00:03:39.298
"Wukong returned," said the Tang Monk.

59
00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.739
"He begged me to let him join us again.

60
00:03:42.539 --> 00:03:44.460
I said no, and then he attacked me!"

61
00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.642
"That's terrible!"

62
00:03:46.902 --> 00:03:47.682
said Wujing.

63
00:03:49.463 --> 00:03:50.464
rotten monkey!"

64
00:03:51.144 --> 00:03:52.485
Bajie stomped his foot.

65
00:03:52.545 --> 00:03:54.926
"We can't let him get away with this!

66
00:03:55.686 --> 00:03:58.308
He probably went home, to the Fruit and Flower Mountain."

67
00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.061
"I'll go there and deal with him," said Wujing.

68
00:04:02.901 --> 00:04:06.422
Bajie gave Wujing directions to the Fruit and Flower Mountain.

69
00:04:11.423 --> 00:04:15.004
When Wujing arrived there, he found Wukong near the waterfall.

70
00:04:19.266 --> 00:04:20.206
shouted Wujing.

71
00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:22.086
"Why did you attack Master?"

72
00:04:23.407 --> 00:04:25.447
monkey looked at Wujing blankly.

73
00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:29.884
"Who are you?"

74
00:04:29.984 --> 00:04:31.105
Wujing raised an eyebrow.

75
00:04:32.206 --> 00:04:33.347
are you talking about?

76
00:04:33.407 --> 00:04:34.587
You know who I am."

77
00:04:34.668 --> 00:04:38.390
"No, I don't," said Wukong.

78
00:04:40.051 --> 00:04:41.072
Sha Wujing!

79
00:04:41.452 --> 00:04:43.253
We were traveling to the West together."

80
00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:47.857
"I'm going to the West but not with you," said Wukong.

81
00:04:48.937 --> 00:04:50.358
pointed to a group of figures.

82
00:04:50.839 --> 00:04:51.639
"I'm going with them."

83
00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:53.921
Wujing looked over.

84
00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:58.404
A monk who looked exactly like the Tang Monk sat on a horse.

85
00:04:59.356 --> 00:05:01.297
A pig stood next to the horse.

86
00:05:01.317 --> 00:05:03.979
"Bajie?" said Wujing.

87
00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:08.702
Just then he saw a purple figure walk over to the horse.

88
00:05:12.025 --> 00:05:14.146
Wujing gasped in shock.
